Finding LOW-1 (V2Review): server_exe() docstring promises `opened: False` on any failure, but an
OSError from os.fstat()/os.read() after a successful open() propagates out of the function instead.

File: tools/kama-llamacpp-live.py, lines 744-758 (second try block has only `finally`, no
`except`); docstring line 736: "any other outcome is `opened: False` with its reason".

Show it:
  python3 - <<'EOF'
  import sys, types
  sys.path.insert(0, 'tools')
  import importlib.util
  spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('live', 'tools/kama-llamacpp-live.py')
  live = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec); spec.loader.exec_module(live)
  real_open, real_fstat = __builtins__.os.open, __builtins__.os.fstat
  import os
  os.open = lambda p, f: 99
  os.fstat = lambda fd: (_ for _ in ()).throw(OSError(5, 'Input/output error'))
  print(live.server_exe(1))   # raises OSError instead of returning opened: False
  EOF
(Conceptual driver; an EIO between open(2) and fstat(2)/read(2) is the trigger.)

Consequence today: main() catches BaseException -> _record_internal, receipt['server_exe'] stays
None -> replay flags `server-exe:absent` (loud, not silent), but the receipt loses the
docstring-promised `opened: False` row and gains an unrelated internal_fault.

Proposed fix (keeps every existing return; finally still closes the fd):
--- a/tools/kama-llamacpp-live.py
+++ b/tools/kama-llamacpp-live.py
@@ -753,7 +753,10 @@
             h.update(chunk)
             left -= len(chunk)
         if left != 0:
             return {'opened': False, 'reason': 'exe-shrank-while-hashed', 'path': path}
+    except OSError as exc:
+        return {'opened': False,
+                'reason': 'exe-read-failed:' + (exc.strerror or type(exc).__name__),
+                'path': path}
     finally:
         os.close(fd)
     return {'opened': True, 'path': path,

